Z||000000||mbramble||01-20-2001||12:59 AM||||Was just watching an old X-files episode -- the one where there was a squad of soldiers who had been operated on so that they never had to sleep.  Quite an asset while they were in Viet Nam, I guess!!  Anyway, as Mulder and Krichek were sitting in traffic on the 'Long Island Freeway' (Expressway maybe), there was a red notchback in front of them.  You could only see in from the front passenger side, not much of a view of the car.  But, the back portion of the center console (between the seats) is pretty unmistakeable.  It had a sunroof and a rear wing.  That's about all you could see of the car.  Anyone ever notice this one before???||||reg||1
Z||000001||Standard||01-20-2001||04:28 AM||||Never saw that one...<P>I was watching a show called "world's worst drivers" or something of that nature on TLC, and they had a section about street racing in Cali.  Had a shot of a parking lot full of cars that was shot from right behind a notchback with a luggage rack, deep green paint.  First Fiero I've seen on TV..||||reg||14
